WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.575
What does this guide implement?

2
00:00:01.575 --> 00:00:05.360
The Federal Modernization
Workbook's Book 08's design,

3
00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:07.800
mapped onto the way Infoblox works.

4
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:13.275
Book 08 wants governed authoritative
DNS and IP address management.

5
00:00:13.275 --> 00:00:17.021
On NIOS that's a Grid: one Grid
Master holds the database,

6
00:00:17.021 --> 00:00:20.850
and every member gets its copy
over an encrypted tunnel.

7
00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:22.050
Part 1 builds it.

8
00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:27.688
Book 08 wants a coexistence period
with Microsoft DNS and DHCP.

9
00:00:27.688 --> 00:00:31.863
On NIOS, managing members
synchronize the Windows servers over

10
00:00:31.863 --> 00:00:35.801
Microsoft's remote procedure
call protocol, read-only first.

11
00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:40.849
Book 08 moves zones and scopes one at
a time; on NIOS that's zone import

12
00:00:40.849 --> 00:00:45.988
by transfer, and a DHCP takeover
done by changing server assignments.

13
00:00:45.988 --> 00:00:51.397
Book 08's default keeps the Active Directory
locator records on AD DNS until the

14
00:00:51.397 --> 00:00:55.659
last domain controller goes, and
this guide keeps that default,

15
00:00:55.659 --> 00:00:59.512
showing NIOS hosting the AD
zone only as the alternative.

16
00:00:59.512 --> 00:01:01.275
Part 2 covers all of that.

17
00:01:01.275 --> 00:01:04.788
Book 08 Chapter 06 requires DNSSEC.

18
00:01:04.788 --> 00:01:08.275
On NIOS, the Grid Master
signs as a hidden primary,

19
00:01:08.275 --> 00:01:12.287
with keys in its database or
a hardware security module.

20
00:01:12.287 --> 00:01:13.412
That's Part 3.

21
00:01:13.412 --> 00:01:17.715
And Chapter 11's evidence becomes
secure syslog to the SIEM,

22
00:01:17.715 --> 00:01:22.287
a copy of the audit log, backups
and the STIG checklist, in Part 4.

23
00:01:22.287 --> 00:01:25.187
Book 08's six phases still govern.

24
00:01:25.187 --> 00:01:27.814
This guide adds a Phase 0 of decisions,

25
00:01:27.814 --> 00:01:31.288
because some NIOS choices
can't be undone cheaply.

26
00:01:31.288 --> 00:01:36.685
Sources: Book 08, Chapters 04
(AD DNS departure), 06 (DNSSEC),

27
00:01:36.685 --> 00:01:42.084
08 (reference architecture),
10 (six phases, cutover loop),

28
00:01:42.084 --> 00:01:49.881
11 (operations and evidence); Infoblox
NIOS 9.1.x About Grids, Managing Microsoft

29
00:01:49.881 --> 00:01:57.860
Windows servers, Importing zone data, DNSSEC
on a Grid; research brief section 10.
